            ("h3", "What Is TPI Screening and Why Does It Matter?"),
            ("p", "TPI stands for Titleist Performance Institute, the body that developed the standard movement screen used by tour coaches and physiotherapists worldwide. The screen is a series of physical tests covering rotation, stability, mobility and balance, and it takes around 45 minutes to work through the full set."),
            ("p", "The point is not to grade your fitness. It is to find the specific restrictions that make certain swing faults almost inevitable. A golfer who cannot separate their hips from their shoulders will slide rather than turn, and no amount of being told to turn will change that until the restriction is addressed. Screening first means the coaching that follows is aimed at something real."),
