            ("p", "Most golfers who use both treat them as different tools. The covered Trackman bays give you volume, numbers and shelter, which makes them the right place to work through the bag or to practise in February. The grass line gives you the real strike and the real lie, which makes it the right place to check that what you built in the bays actually survives contact with turf."),
            ("p", "A common routine is to warm up and gather numbers in a bay, then move out to the grass for the last twenty balls to confirm the strike is genuine. Finish on the <a href=\"short-game.html\">short game area</a> and you have covered every part of the game in a single visit, without moving your car."),
