            ("p", "The turf line runs through the playing season, broadly spring to autumn, and closes when the ground is too wet or too worn to give a fair lie. Managing it that way is what keeps the surface worth hitting from. When it is closed, the covered bays carry on seven days a week, so a wasted journey is never a risk if you check before you set off."),
            ("p", "Warming up before a round is the other job the grass line does particularly well. Ten minutes off turf before you tee off tells you what your strike is doing that morning far more honestly than the same ten minutes off a mat, and it is the reason a lot of Ormonde Fields members walk past the bays on their way to the first tee."),
